# APP-SPLIT-003D — gates log (2026-11-26)

Slice of APP-SPLIT-001 (RUN-2 resume recipe): the home header/Today wiring
slice extracted from App() into `apps/desktop/src/app/home-wiring.ts` as a
pure move. Boundaries: the session-lifecycle handlers the Today header (and
the session chrome sharing its state) wires — the slice the RUN-2 recipe
left as the last 003 sibling. openPractice stays App-owned (practice
surface, next slice candidate) and is passed into the slice as a callback.

## What moved (verbatim; pure-move check below)

- `runStartSession(deps)` — the `startSession` body (queue snapshot,
  measured clock start, first openPractice).
- `runAdvanceSession(deps, counted)` — the `advanceSession` body (bridge,
  auto-advance, finish, capstone close).
- `runCloseSession(deps, reason)` / `runPauseSession(deps)` /
  `runResumeSession(deps)` — stop/pause/resume bodies.
- `runStartCapstoneSession(deps, node)` / `runFinishCapstoneSession(deps)` —
  the UNIT-CAPSTONE-001 section-review flow riding the same runner.
- `publishSession`, `sessionOutcomeFrom`, `isSessionRunnable` — the shared
  session-outcome helpers (module-private calls, deps passed through).
- `HomeWiringDeps` + `SessionQueue` — the props bundle (render values +
  setters + App-owned refs + callbacks); App() builds `sessionWiringDeps`
  once per render and passes it at each call site.

App.tsx keeps owning every hook (session/capstone/practice state, all
refs, the bridge state machine), `openPractice` and all other practice
wiring, `changeBudget`/`setKanaKeyboardSetting` (settings-owned), the path-
state derivation, and all JSX. Thin wrappers (`advanceSession`,
`closeSession`, `pauseSession`, `resumeSession`) keep every JSX and
history-wiring call site unchanged. No test, gate script, or behavior pin
was touched. Test tree swept for `from "./App"` imports: all point at the
primitives re-export shim (App.test.tsx) or `App` itself
(journeys/harness, history-screens, mobile-screens, serve-banner.test) —
untouched by this slice, no re-exports added or removed.

